\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Theorem}
\title{Fermion integration updates the connection weight}
\date{2026-11-10}

\p{Let the \vocabk{massive graded Wilson data}{fdip-00IN} be given, with the determinant bounds and positive normalizer #{Z} of \ref{fdip-00IP}, and with the fixed-connection and coupled coefficient functionals of the [coupled coefficient functional](fdip-00IT). Let #{X} be the link configuration space, let #{A} be the algebra of #{\mathcal A(\mathcal V)}-valued functions on #{X} with bounded Borel coefficients and pointwise exterior product, and let #{B} be the algebra of scalar bounded Borel functions. The outer algebra is the constant scalars inside #{B}. Define
##{P(F)(U)=J_{\mathcal V}(F(U)),\qquad
w(U)=e^{\theta_{K_U}},\qquad
Q(b)=\int_X w_g(U)b(U)\,d\lambda(U),}
and define #{D} independently by
##{D(F)=J_{\mathcal V}\Bigl(\int_X w_g(U)F(U)\,d\lambda(U)\Bigr),}
with the integral taken coefficientwise. Then #{D=Q\circ P}, the marginal #{z(U)=\det K_U} is a unit of #{B}, and #{t=Z} is a unit of #{\mathbb C}. \ref{fdip-00KX} gives
##{\begin{aligned}
E_{A,B}(F)(U)&=(\det K_U)^{-1}J_{\mathcal V}\bigl(F(U)e^{\theta_{K_U}}\bigr),\\
E_{B,\mathbb C}(b)&=Z^{-1}\int_X w_g(U)\det K_U\,b(U)\,d\lambda(U),
\end{aligned}}
and #{E_{B,\mathbb C}\circ E_{A,B}} is the coupled coefficient functional.}

\proof{
\p{The paired coefficient #{J_{\mathcal V}} is linear on the finitely many coefficients, so it passes inside the coefficientwise integral. This is #{D=Q\circ P}. The bound #{m^n\le\det K_U\le M^n} puts both #{\det K_U} and its reciprocal in #{B}, and the paired integral gives #{P(w)(U)=\det K_U}. The outer marginal #{Q(z)} equals #{Z}. The first display is the fixed-connection functional. The second is integration against the connection law of \ref{fdip-00IP}. In the composite, #{\det K_U} cancels, and the gauge factor #{w_g} remains in the outer integral, leaving the coupled coefficient functional.}
}
